# Graph Builder Role

You receive a list of source files from a single module (directory) and their
contents. Respond with exactly two tagged lines — no prose, no preamble, nothing else.

## Output format

```
GRAPH_SUMMARY:<one paragraph — what this module does and why it exists>
GRAPH_SUBSYSTEM:<single word grouping — e.g. auth, billing, api, storage, graph, wiki, cli>
```

Rules:
- GRAPH_SUMMARY: one paragraph, no bullets, plain prose
- GRAPH_SUBSYSTEM: one word only
- Output exactly these two lines. Nothing else.


Module path: frontends
Files:

--- frontends/eslint-base.cjs (59 lines) ---
// Shared ESLint 8 legacy base for every frontends/* workspace.
//
// Only genuinely common configuration lives here — parser, base plugin
// extends, react settings, and the two rules every workspace agreed on
// (react-in-jsx-scope off, no-unused-vars with the `^_` args convention).
//
// jsx-a11y is in the base `extends`/`plugins` because its recommended set was
// adopted byte-identically by all 17 workspaces. What it does NOT own is the
// test-fixture relaxation of the a11y interaction/role rules: those globs
// differ per workspace (`tests/**` for most, `src/**/__tests__/**` for
// ask-mfe), so each workspace keeps that `overrides` block itself.
// Anything that legitimately differs per workspace (no-restricted-imports
// for the Radix contract, react/jsx-no-literals and its allowedStrings,
// per-workspace overrides for test files, extra ignorePatterns) stays in
// that workspace's own .eslintrc.cjs — do not fold those in here, and do
// not add a rule here that would change any workspace's effective rule set
// beyond what this file documents.
module.exports = {
  env: { browser: true, es2022: true },
  extends: [
    'eslint:recommended',
    'plugin:@typescript-eslint/recommended',
    'plugin:react/recommended',
    'plugin:react-hooks/recommended',
    'plugin:jsx-a11y/recommended',
  ],
  parser: '@typescript-eslint/parser',
  parserOptions: { ecmaVersion: 'latest', sourceType: 'module' },
  plugins: ['@typescript-eslint', 'react', 'react-hooks', 'jsx-a11y'],
  settings: { react: { version: '18.3' } },
  rules: {
    'react/react-in-jsx-scope': 'off',
    '@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars': ['error', { argsIgnorePattern: '^_' }],
    // Structurally forbids `m[...]` computed lookups against the Paraglide
    // message namespace. Paraglide v2 emits each message as an individually
    // named export, not an indexable object, so any computed access on `m`
    // defeats tree-shaking for the whole namespace regardless of how the
    // computed key is typed — a 4-member union cast still broke it, which is
    // why this is a syntax-level ban rather than a type-level one. Replace a
    // computed lookup with an explicit Record of named message references,
    // as done in frontends/studio-mfe/src/config/studioTasks.ts:1-11.
    'no-restricted-syntax': [
      'error',
      {
        selector: "MemberExpression[computed=true][object.name='m']",
        message:
          'Do not index the Paraglide message namespace with a computed ' +
          "expression (m[...]). Paraglide emits each message as its own " +
          'named export, so a computed lookup on `m` defeats tree-shaking ' +
          'for every message in the bundle, even when the key is typed. ' +
          'Build an explicit Record mapping each case to its named message ' +
          'function reference instead — see the fix pattern documented at ' +
          'frontends/studio-mfe/src/config/studioTasks.ts:1-11.',
      },
    ],
  },
  ignorePatterns: ['dist', 'node_modules'],
}



